    "vernacular": "Flat Sudano-Sahelian savanna capital on red laterite earth: one- to three-storey flat-roofed cement-block and banco houses rendered in cream, white, ochre or sand-red behind plastered walls, many compounds roofed in rust corrugated sheet; broad avenues and roundabouts crowned with sculptural monuments from the Sankara era onward; banco-built colonial landmarks such as the cathedral; 1980s Chinese-built institutions; concrete-and-glass offices and the Ouaga 2000 district for government.",
